ing Washington operations.\n\nThe expansion comes as Qatar faces severe economic pressure from the war with Iran, which has damaged its energy infrastructure and disrupted liquefied natural gas exports. Government spending fell 14% in the first half of 2026, while overseas aid funding was reduced by approximately 85%.\n\nAl Jazeera has for so long provided a platform for Islamist movements, particularly the Muslim Brotherhood. Its Arabic-language network prominently featured the late Yusuf al-Qaradawi, the Qatar-based cleric and influential Muslim Brotherhood-associated ideologue, whose religious program Sharia and Life reached audiences across the Arab world.\n\nAl Jazeera also uses its international, particularly Western reach, to normalize Islamist political narratives among Western audiences, while giving sympathetic coverage to radical-left movements and causes."},"possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":8,"impression_count":14551,"like_count":57,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":14,"retweet_count":14},"text":"Qatar is pressing ahead with a major expansion of its state-owned Al Jazeera media network despite a 42% decline in government revenue during the first half of 2026 and reported operating-budget cuts of up to 30% across government departments.\n\nThe network announced on October 29 https://t.co/AQpkYSbbHw","url":"https://x.com/visegrad24/status/2119263647340044599"},{"author_id":"1243560408025198593","conversation_id":"2119263619649315072","created_at":"2026-11-08T02:59:55.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2119263619649315072"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":18,"id":"20280088","start":3,"username":"MacFarlaneNews"}]},"id":"2119263619649315072","lang":"en","possibly_sensitive":false,"public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":2449,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":44},"referenced_tweets":[{"id":"2119262338121359533","type":"retweeted"}],"text":"RT @MacFarlaneNews: The midterms were a brutal condemnat